{{!
  @template mod_googlemeet/google_login_button

  Button that opens the Google OAuth login in a popup window.

  The login URL travels in data-loginurl (escaped by Mustache) and mod_googlemeet/google_login opens
  it on click, so no URL value is interpolated into inline JavaScript. The caller initialises that
  module with buttonid.

  Context variables required for this template:
  * buttonid - Unique id of the button, passed to mod_googlemeet/google_login init().
  * loginurl - Plain (unescaped) Google OAuth login URL.

  Example context (json):
  {
    "buttonid": "googlemeet_login_1",
    "loginurl": "https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/v2/auth?client_id=c&response_type=code"
  }
}}
<div class="mt-2"><button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="{{buttonid}}" data-loginurl="{{loginurl}}">{{#str}} logintoaccount, mod_googlemeet {{/str}}</button></div>
